    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, led by the optimal synergy between **Josh Naylor** (78.46) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21). Both benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Littell and Imai, respectively; **Vinnie Pasquantino** in particular sees a massive 14% boost from a favorable platoon split, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on an elite 19% SP skill advantage. We are also leaning heavily on the elite sprint speed and top-of-the-order positioning of **Corbin Carroll** (72.85), who, despite the platoon disadvantage against Lodolo, remains a mandatory start due to his ability to single-handedly sustain our SB category dominance. **James Wood** remains a high-floor anchor at 59.85, bolstered by an elite 0.403 xwOBA that justifies his start despite a slightly lower SP skill rating.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Brice Turang** (48.67), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient situational play of **Jose Caballero**. While **Brice Turang** offers high-end speed, the combination of a tough matchup against Banks and a defensive disadvantage behind the plate pushed his efficiency below our current starters. We are also keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki**, whose score of 52.32 is tentative pending his official placement in the lineup; should he drop down the order, we are prepared to pivot to one of our reserves. We remain cautious with **Max Muncy** (51.37) and **Travis Bazzana** (49.16), both of whom are operating near our floor threshold, though their platoon advantages against Sullivan and Flaherty provide just enough leverage to keep them in the starting nine for today\u2019s volume.",
